<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Westminster</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Westminster is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraser-river">Fraser River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-columbia">British Columbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. Royal Engineers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-clement-moody">Richard Clement Moody</a> founded it in 1859 as the capital of the mainland Colony of British Columbia. It remained capital of the united colony until 1868, when Victoria was chosen instead after a bitter rivalry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-westminster.jpg" alt="New Westminster" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Northwest · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Westminster_platform_level.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
